\ poseidon2.fam — the node's Poseidon2 and Merkle paths (docs/NODE.md, step
\ 2), after arith.fam.  As tabminer's miner/src/poseidon2.rs and merkle.rs:
\ width 16 over BabyBear, x^7, 8 full rounds and 13 partial, bit-compatible
\ with Plonky3's default_babybear_poseidon2_16; values in Montgomery form
\ (arith.fam).
\
\ perm16 is one raw word (from tools/genposeidon.py, which reads tabminer's
\ round constants): the S-box's four products (x^2, x^3, x^6, x^7) are its
\ only ones, since the internal layer's diagonal is small multiples and
\ powers of 1/2 (1/2^27 = -15).
\
\ compress: the first 8 words of perm(a || b), the Merkle node.  hash: the
\ sponge with rate 8, the length in the first capacity word, a short last
\ block zero padded (none empty: one permutation).  mroot and mverify: a
\ leaf row's root from its path, siblings from the leaf up.  Not
\ reentrant: they share p2s and the variables below.

: p2s variable ;               \ the state: 16 words
: mvt variable ;               \ mverify's root: 8 words
: p2init  arinit p2s @ 0= if 40 lit alloc p2s !  20 lit alloc mvt ! then ;

\ perm16 ( s -- )  the 16 words at s permuted in place.
: perm16 sqt @
83280100 ,   \ lw a7,0(sp)   ( the table )
03274100 ,   \ lw a4,4(sp)   ( the state )
13018100 ,   \ addi sp,sp,8
EF10007E ,   \ jal ra,p2_ext   ( the first external layer )
